thermal: qcom: tsens: drop __init from the init callbacks

The probe can be deferred (it waits for clocks/nvmem on yupik). When it runs after the
module's init sections were freed, priv->ops->init points into freed memory that the next
module reuses: on the A52s (2026-11-12) the call landed in qcom_ipcc_irq_fn and kCFI killed
the kernel ("CFI failure at tsens_probe+0x1a8 ... target: qcom_ipcc_irq_fn+0x9c").

diff --color -ru tsens-orig/tsens.c b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
--- tsens-orig/tsens.c	2026-11-12 20:25:40.459975925 +0200
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c	2026-11-12 20:25:40.460735114 +0200
@@ -1047,7 +1047,7 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
-int __init init_common(struct tsens_priv *priv)
+int init_common(struct tsens_priv *priv)
 {
 	void __iomem *tm_base, *srot_base;
 	struct device *dev = priv->dev;
